<title>AUSTRALIA: AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES - Tenders total A$85 mln.</title>
<headline>AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES - Tenders total A$85 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian commercial paper market saw three promissory notes tenders totalling A$85 million on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The largest was for Lend Lease, which brought a A$40 million offering of May 20 dated paper and fetched a yield of 6.05 percent.</p>
<p>Traders said that yields at the short end of the Australian curve continued to be eroded on the realisation that it will be some months before the Reserve Bank follows the Federal Reserve into a tightening cycle based on current domestic fundamentals.</p>
<p>The June bill futures contract has rallied in the past couple of weeks and back to 94.00 this morning, in line with current 6.0 percent cash rates, having discounted a 25 basis point tightening in early March.</p>
